  "worked_solution": "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\nP(X=1\\,|\\,Y=6)=\\frac{P(X=1,Y=6)}{P(Y=6)}=\\frac{f(1,6)}{{f}_{Y}(6)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(6) & =f(1,6)+f(3,6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(1,6)=\\frac{1}{4}.$ \n\nFinally, substituting ${f}_{Y}(6)=\\frac{3}{8}$ and $f(1,6)=\\frac{1}{4}$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1\\,|\\,Y=6) & =\\frac{f(1,6)}{{f}_{Y}(6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{4})}{(\\frac{3}{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
